   {
    "id": "h5_00013",
    "type": "h5",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     37,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[A32][/A32]Printing to Standard Output",
    "placeholders": {
     "A32": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_177_06_01\" id=\"tag_17_177_06_01\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00014",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     37,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The following example gets the current time, converts it to a string using [A33][I34]localtime[/I34]()[/A33] and [A35][I36]asctime[/I36]()[/A35], and prints it to\nstandard output using [I37]fputs[/I37](). It then prints the number of minutes to an event for which it is waiting.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A33": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/localtime.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I34": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A35": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/asctime.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I36": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I37": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00015",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     39
    ],
    "text": "[A38][/A38]APPLICATION USAGE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A38": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_177_07\" id=\"tag_17_177_07\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00016",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [A39][I40]puts[/I40]()[/A39] function appends a &lt;newline&gt; while [I41]fputs[/I41]() does not.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A39": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/puts.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I40": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I41": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00017",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     3
    ],
    "text": "This volume of POSIX.1-2024 requires that successful completion simply return a non-negative integer. There are at least three\nknown different implementation conventions for this requirement:",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00018",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     5,
     1,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Return a constant value.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00019",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     5,
     3,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Return the last character written.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00020",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     5,
     5,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Return the number of bytes written. Note that this implementation convention cannot be adhered to for strings longer than\n{INT_MAX} bytes as the value would not be representable in the return type of the function. For backwards-compatibility,\nimplementations can return the number of bytes for strings of up to {INT_MAX} bytes, and return {INT_MAX} for all longer\nstrings.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00021",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     43
    ],
    "text": "[A42][/A42]RATIONALE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A42": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_177_08\" id=\"tag_17_177_08\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00022",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I43]fputs[/I43]() function is one whose source code was specified in the referenced [I44]The C Programming Language[/I44]. In the\noriginal edition, the function had no defined return value, yet many practical implementations would, as a side-effect, return the\nvalue of the last character written as that was the value remaining in the accumulator used as a return value. In the second\nedition of the book, either the fixed value 0 or EOF would be returned depending upon the return value of [A45][I46]ferror[/I46]()[/A45]; however, for compatibility with extant implementations, several implementations\nwould, upon success, return a positive value representing the last byte written.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I43": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I44": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A45": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/ferror.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I46": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
